    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d600">

                <pb facs="0688" n="672" xml:id="pg672"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">822.01/9–747: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Embassy in Ecuador
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-08T13:00:00-04:00">September 8,
                            1947—1 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>266. Urtel 388, Sept 7.<anchor n="14"
                        xml:id="d600-f1"/> Dept does not wish to take any action in respect of
                    Ecuadoran recognition at this time. Situation is not yet considered clear and it
                    is considered preferable to await developments particularly from Sept 15 meeting
                    of Congress and in general to have clear picture of whether regime manifests all
                    qualities of stable <hi rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> govt. Also we will
                    probably wish to await views of a rather substantial body of other American
                    republics.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
